speechtext:
Madam Speaker, I am pleased and honoured to present a petition on behalf of 87 students and staff of St. James Collegiate located in my riding of Winnipeg St. James.
This petition relates to the environment and specifically the Rafferty-Alameda dams project in Saskatchewan. The petition reads as follows:
Whereas the courts have ruled that a full environmental review must be conducted on the Rafferty-Alameda dams project in Saskatchewan;
Whereas construction on the Rafferty-Alameda dams project should have stopped during this environmental review;
Whereas construction has now resumed upon this project without an environmental assessment having been completed; and
Whereas this project may have serious repercussions upon the environment, including fish, migratory birds and the lands of the province of Manitoba and the federal government;
Wherefore, the undersigned, your petitioners humbly pray and call upon Parliament to take every possible action to stop construction on the Rafferty-Alameda dams project and to ensure that a full environmental assessment is conducted.
I would like to congratulate the students and staff of St. James Collegiate on their initiative. I thank them for caring, and we are all very proud of them.
